diff --git a/changelog.d/cli-v-prefix.feature.rst b/changelog.d/cli-v-prefix.feature.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..154317b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/cli-v-prefix.feature.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+Every ``pysemver`` subcommand now accepts an optional leading ``v`` or ``V``
+on its version arguments (for example ``v1.4.2`` from a git tag). The output
+is printed without the prefix.
diff --git a/changelog.d/compare-dict.deprecation.rst b/changelog.d/compare-dict.deprecation.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6c740e9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/compare-dict.deprecation.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+Passing a ``dict`` to ``Version.compare()`` is deprecated and now emits a
+``DeprecationWarning``. Pass a ``str``, ``tuple``, ``list`` or ``Version``
+instead (for example ``Version(**mydict)``). Comparison operators such as ``==``
+are not affected.
diff --git a/changelog.d/next-version-token.deprecation.rst b/changelog.d/next-version-token.deprecation.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..be7f4b7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/next-version-token.deprecation.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+``Version.next_version()`` now names its keyword ``token``, matching
+``bump_prerelease()`` and ``bump_build()``. The old ``prerelease_token=``
+keyword still works and is deprecated, but emits no warning.
